findings.claim:
The first draft had already dropped the 'adventuress' sentence. The revision then cuts:
- the 'proved I have some wits to live by' punchline;
- her sitting up 'thoroughly well in hand';
- the impossible-sum reasoning before 'a little something down';
- Whittington's 'meek little kid with just enough brains for my purpose'.

The revision cuts:
- Tuppence's recognition of Madame Colombier's and 'more than ever puzzled';
- 'Details about your past life in England might be more difficult to sustain';
- 'I could doubtless obtain some one else for very much less';
- 'She felt that Whittington had scored.'
